{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GCJDpK1EzTG48o99VDSuM1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** â€” a single-folder, stdlib-only personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown a substantial R&D \"trio orchestration\" layer on top of a markdown task manager.\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a personal productivity/task dashboard.** Anchor is a self-contained Python app (`anchor_gui.py`) that reads and writes plain-markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) as the single source of truth â€” tracking tasks through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored) with priorities, energy, due dates, and notes.\n\n- **Ships as a persistent local web server.** It runs as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777`, serving a fully interactive browser dashboard (check tasks done, add tasks, capture ideas) that saves straight to the markdown files. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Self-tests itself daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint and the full task lifecycle, plus walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed â€” never live `claude`), and writes a dated health report.\n\n- **It has become an R&D \"mission control\" / \"project cockpit\" for the trio.** The bulk of recent work ships a per-project control surface for the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio: each project window shows lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers) as status-lit tiles, with cached/validated session summaries, per-lane doc roles, and a cost/tokens/time rollup.\n\n- **Real interactive terminals with isolation.** v3/v4 ship live ConPTY terminal sessions (via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, lazily imported) over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport with xterm.js, each session isolated in its own git worktree+branch, with a durable session registry, engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), stage handoffs between plan and build, and ephemeral deliverable previews hard-guarded never to bind port 8777.\n\n- **Constraints that define it.** Single folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), no database, no syncing, Python stdlib only (sole exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals), all artifacts human-readable/plain-text â€” enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan. Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\".\n\nThis summary is drawn from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decision anchors in `planning/rnd-v3` and `planning/rnd-v4`; the v4 \"Project Cockpit\" is recorded as built (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) and merged to master."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"877afbb6-6bef-4f3d-ac8e-dee741b0ad9b","uuid":"7cbe024e-5e91-4578-aca0-b78a103bffaf","request_id":"req_011Cc1vqz5gjscr9AkMHYmXL"}
